From: punktfunk <packages@unom.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:44:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/44] pipewire: declare an exported LINEAR capture image
 external on Intel

A capture dmabuf that takes no modifier is a plain VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR
image. Its allocation asks for export, but the image never says its
memory is external, and since "keep dmabuf capture buffers in device
memory" it is no longer host-visible either.

Intel's driver places such an image for itself alone. From Xe2 (Lunar
Lake, Battlemage) its first device-local memory type is compressed, and
every image that is neither declared external nor modifier-tiled may use
it. The consumer imports DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, which is uncompressed, and
reads the bytes as they lie: an Arc B580 host streamed the capture's NV12
as 256-pixel runs of noise with a green tail.

On Intel, chain VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo on an exported LINEAR
image. The driver then keeps it out of compressed memory and gives it no
auxiliary surface. Its dmabuf export is defined for LINEAR tiling. AMD's
is defined for modifiers only, and NVIDIA's captures stay as they are.
---
 src/rendervulkan.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index 433cd15..abfd001 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -2608,7 +2608,12 @@ bool CVulkanTexture::BInit( uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t depth, uin
 		};
 	}
 	
-	if ( pDMA != nullptr )
+	// On Intel an exported LINEAR image says it is a dmabuf, as an imported one does. Its driver
+	// places an image it was not told about for itself alone: in compressed memory from Xe2,
+	// and the importer of a LINEAR dmabuf reads those bytes as they lie.
+	static constexpr uint32_t k_uIntelVendorID = 0x8086;
+	const bool bExportsLinear = flags.bExportable && !flags.bFlippable && tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR && g_device.vendorID() == k_uIntelVendorID;
+	if ( pDMA != nullptr || bExportsLinear )
 	{
 		externalImageCreateInfo = {
 			.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_IMAGE_CREATE_INFO,
